      "id": 1,
      "text": "Old Northside received historic designation in late 1978 after adopting a plan for preserving architecture and history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Northside_Historic_District",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood was the original site of Butler University, then North Western Christian University, before moving to Irvington.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Northside_Historic_District",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1979, the Old Northside Neighborhood Association formed to preserve historic architecture and host cultural events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Northside_Historic_District",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The President Benjamin Harrison Home and the Morris-Butler House, both on the National Register, are open for tours in Old Northside.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Northside_Historic_District",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The former Central Avenue Methodist Church was restored in 2010–2011 into the Indiana Landmarks Center, a performance venue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Northside_Historic_District",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
